# Configs such as db connection Configs
This folder holds all environment-specific settings. Instead of scattering process.env calls across your codebase, you import a single config object.

index.js – Reads .env variables, validates them (consider using a library like envalid or zod), and exports a frozen config object.
database.js – Database connection logic (MongoDB, PostgreSQL, etc.).
logger.js – Logger setup (Winston, Pino, or similar).